Keep the queued shader compiles when the pipeline cache goes

0009 made ~PipelineCache drop the work no worker had started, on both its
queues. A pipeline build a worker has already started waits for its shaders
(GraphicsPipeline::Build, Shader::WaitDone): with that shader's compile still
queued and dropped, nothing ever marks it done, the build waits for ever, and
so does the destructor waiting for the build. A quit or a reset (System::
Shutdown, the renderer destroyed) while a new scene compiles hung the app.
Found by reading (audit 2026-10-20), not seen on a device.

Only the pipeline builds are dropped now; the shaders' queue runs to its end.
A shader is a short SPIR-V compile; the pipelines were the seconds 0009 saved.

--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -152,7 +152,11 @@
     // after a boot otherwise waited for every pipeline the boot had queued from the disk
     // cache, each a whole Metal compile on MoltenVK (seconds on a phone).
     pipeline_workers.CancelPending();
-    shader_workers.CancelPending();
+    // Not the shaders': a pipeline build a worker has already started waits for
+    // its shaders (GraphicsPipeline::Build, WaitDone), and a dropped shader is
+    // never marked done, so that build, and this destructor waiting for it,
+    // would wait for ever. A shader is a short SPIR-V compile; the pipelines
+    // were the seconds.
     pipeline_workers.WaitForRequests();
     shader_workers.WaitForRequests();
     SaveDriverPipelineDiskCache();
